= The Fourth Congress

The Fourth Congress of the International closes in Moscow on 5 December. Lenin, partly paralysed since his first stroke, spoke for an hour in November and told the delegates their resolutions were too Russian for foreigners to understand.

For the German delegation the question was the workers' government. Radek and Ernst Meyer argued that a government of the workers' parties, even one formed in a parliament, could be a step towards power. Ruth Fischer answered that a workers' government could only be another name for the dictatorship of the proletariat. Zinoviev's resolution allows for both. [? if e22_fc_directive = 1 : Radek has drafted the instruction to the German party himself, and it expects results by the spring. ?]

- @broad: Take home Radek's reading.
- @narrow: Take home Fischer's reading.
- @own: Say the German party will decide what it means in Germany.

@broad
subtitle: The road to Saxony and to coalition offers is open. Radek is pleased.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_fourth_congress = 1;
RG.comply(35);
RG.ecci('radek', 8);
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 6;
Q.lean_unionist += 3;
!}

The Zentrale's report says it plainly: the party will offer the SPD a workers' government wherever the two parties have a majority.

@narrow
subtitle: The Left is encouraged. Zinoviev and Bukharin approve.
view-if: offensive_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_fourth_congress = 2;
RG.comply(10);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 6);
RG.ecci('bukharin', 6);
RG.ecci('radek', -6);
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 6;
Q.lean_offensive += 3;
!}

Fischer comes back to Berlin and tells the district that the workers' government is a slogan for the street, not for the Landtag.

@own
subtitle: More independence. Moscow will want to know what it means, and will give us two more months to explain.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_fourth_congress = 3;
RG.stall(2);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -6);
Q.independence += 8;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
!}

[? if luxemburg_alive = 1 : Rosa Luxemburg, who did not go to Moscow, writes the German resolution herself. ?][? if luxemburg_alive = 0 : Clara Zetkin's report says the German party will choose its own allies. ?] Zinoviev calls it federalism and lets it pass.
